WEBVTT

00:00:00.00 --> 00:00:05.00
The Song dynasty was an era of rapid urban growth in Chinese history.

00:00:05.00 --> 00:00:12.00
As commerce developed, people needed more convenient ways to spread information.

00:00:12.00 --> 00:00:17.00
Printing technology therefore became more and more important.

00:00:17.00 --> 00:00:25.00
Craftsmen first carved characters into wooden blocks, then applied ink and printed the text onto paper.

00:00:25.00 --> 00:00:32.00
Later, the appearance of movable-type printing allowed characters to be rearranged and reused.

00:00:32.00 --> 00:00:39.00
More and more people could buy books, read, and learn new knowledge.

00:00:39.00 --> 00:00:47.00
Song commerce was also highly developed; the markets held not only goods and books.

00:00:47.00 --> 00:00:52.00
People also began to use paper money, which made trade more convenient.

00:00:53.00 --> 00:00:59.00
Cities, commerce, and new technologies changed people's lives.

00:00:59.00 --> 00:01:08.00
These inventions influenced not only the Song dynasty; they also had a profound impact on later China and the world.
